                "headline": "Flood Watch issued September 5 at 4:31PM MDT until September 6 at 3:00AM MDT by NWS Denver CO",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of northeast Colorado, including the following\ncounties, Logan County, Phillips County and Sedgwick County.\n\n* WHEN...Until 3 AM MDT Sunday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Scattered to numerous thunderstorms are expected to repeatedly\nmove across far northeast Colorado this evening and into the\nearly morning hours. Locally, up to 3 to 5 inches of rainfall is\npossible.",
